---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: help_of(line)
---
Copy a board; it prints the copy with its link.
The copy keeps the objects; its rights are not copied unless --rights is given.

USAGE
  holst board cp <board> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board to copy

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws    The workspace a new thing goes to: id or part of its name; needed when you have several
      --name name       The copy's name; "<name>-copy" by default, as in the web app
      --folder folder   The folder the copy goes into: a folder id, link or part of its name; / is the root; the board's own folder by default
      --rights          Copy the board's rights too
  -n, --dry-run         Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst b cp "Roadmap"
  $ holst b cp "Roadmap" --name "Roadmap Q4" --folder "Plans" --rights

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
